    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c1_coefficient_resultant_elimination",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=1 mismatch packet is one coefficient resultant",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "Let D_*(Y)=Y^4-e_1Y^3+e_2Y^2-e_3Y+e_4 split with distinct nonzero roots. For ordered distinct roots A,C, set S=e_1-A-C, P=e_4/(AC), and Nhat(A,C)=(AC)^6 N(A;S,P), where N is the radical-free c=1 norm. Then Nhat is polynomial of bidegree at most (18,18). With H(A,C)=(D_*(C)-D_*(A))/(C-A), the twelve c=1 candidates pass iff Res_A(D_*(A),Res_C(H(A,C),Nhat(A,C)))=0. This resultant equals e_4^36 times the product of all twelve norms, so it is an exact coefficient-only constant-degree compiler, not an exclusion.",
